The desktop, Android and Web account transport uses CyberBus. The CyberBus
workspace is MIT OR Apache-2.0, but its `cyberbus-transport` crate is
LGPL-3.0-or-later and the vendored EasyTier component is LGPL-3.0. AnyWork
statically links that transport in native builds. The browser overlay runtime
embeds EasyTier's LGPL-3.0 core WASM.

Complete license texts are in licenses/cyberbus-MIT.txt,
licenses/cyberbus-Apache-2.0.txt, licenses/cyberbus-transport-LGPL-3.0.txt,
licenses/GPL-3.0.txt, licenses/easytier-LGPL-3.0.txt and
licenses/easytier-js-Apache-2.0.txt. The exact CyberBus v0.2.0 commit
a2b5be3b2c3cd8d21e6a0c5bf2b4da2040f36c11 and EasyTier v2.7.1 commit
0d9c52b169dc2112687ddefcf571cd01d383193c, their build and relink instructions,
and the browser WASM provenance are shipped in
artifacts/corresponding-source.tar.gz, scripts/corresponding-source.py,
scripts/build-easytier-browser.sh and
web/public/easytier-browser.PROVENANCE.json. Do not describe the combined
transport as MIT/Apache-only, and do not prohibit reverse engineering for
debugging modifications to the LGPL portion.
See licenses/cyberbus-LGPL-COMPLIANCE.md for the release checklist.

